tar from sbase, the suckless base utilities (MIT licence), taken from
https://git.suckless.org/sbase at commit
c546c3a5724c81cee9a11d816a38ccdf17472129
on 2026-09-06 with tools/fetch_tar.sh.

Copied without modification:
  src/          tar.c, tar.1 and the headers arg.h, fs.h, util.h, text.h,
                utf.h, queue.h
  src/libutil/  the whole utility library; user/Makefile compiles only
                eprintf.c, ealloc.c, reallocarray.c, mkdirp.c, recurse.c
                and strlcpy.c, the files tar.c needs
  LICENSE, README, Makefile  the upstream licence, readme and build file
                (the build file is not used)

sbase's Makefile generates a compat.h that util.h includes; user/Makefile
writes an empty one into build/user/tar/. strlcpy.c is compiled with
-Dstrlcpy=sbase_strlcpy so that its definition does not collide with the
libc one. The vendored files are exempt from the minios line count and
naming conventions. See docs/design/artar.md.
